10:["$","p",null,{"children":["Port 50061 is the one that turns a cache into a compromise. A process that can\nopen a gRPC connection to it can call ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ConnectWorker"}],", be added to the\nscheduler's pool, and start receiving actions, including the compiler\ninvocations, the secrets in your action environments, and the outputs that get\nwritten back into the CAS under digests your developers will later trust."]}]
11:["$","p",null,{"children":"No handshake exists beyond the protocol's own. The scheduler does not check\nwho is connecting, because there is nothing to check with."}]
12:["$","p",null,{"children":"Three consequences, in order of how often they bite:"}]
13:["$","p",null,{"children":["An attacker who can reach 50061 can ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"register a malicious worker"}]," and be\nhanded real actions. Whatever those actions can see, they can see."]}]
14:["$","p",null,{"children":["An attacker who can reach 50061 can ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"poison the cache"}],", because a worker\nuploads action results and the CAS accepts them. A poisoned result for a\nwidely-cached action propagates to every developer who gets a cache hit on it."]}]
15:["$","p",null,{"children":["An attacker who can reach 50061 can ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"denial-of-service the scheduler"}]," by\nregistering and disconnecting, since each disconnect requeues that worker's\nin-flight actions and, in this tree, consumes one of their retries."]}]
16:["$","p",null,{"children":"What to do:"}]
17:["$","p",null,{"children":["Bind it to an address only workers can reach. The single-host Compose file gets\nthis right (the scheduler's 50061 is not published to the host at all; workers\nreach it over the Compose network) and\n",["$","$L58",null,{"href":"/operate/deploy-docker-compose#the-multi-worker-variant","children":"the multi-worker variant"}],"\ndoes not; it publishes ",["$","code",null,{"children":"50061:50061"}]," on all interfaces. Fix that before running\nit anywhere routable."]}]
18:["$","p",null,{"children":["On Kubernetes, keep 50061 off any ",["$","code",null,{"children":"GRPCRoute"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Ingress"}],", and add a\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"NetworkPolicy"}]," that admits only the worker pods, since nothing else stops a\npod in another namespace from dialling the Service directly."]}]
19:["$","p",null,{"children":["On ",["$","$L58",null,{"href":"/operate/deploy-bare-metal","children":"bare metal"}],", bind it to the private interface or\nfirewall it. It should never appear in a load balancer."]}]
1a:["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-admin-endpoint-has-no-authentication","children":"The admin endpoint has no authentication"}]
1b:["$","p",null,{"children":["The admin REST API registers under ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/admin"}]," by default. Every shipped example\nthat enables it puts it on the worker API listener; one\n(",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge-config/examples/worker_with_redis_scheduler.json5"}],") also enables it\non the public listener, which is the thing not to copy. Its only route is:"]}]
