1f:["$","p",null,{"children":["The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"health"}]," service is on the same footing: path ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," by default, five\nsecond timeout, no authentication. It leaks less, but it is another reason the\n50061 listener belongs on a private network rather than behind an\nauthentication proxy you have not written."]}]
20:["$","div",null,{"className":"my-6 flex gap-3 rounded-xl border px-5 py-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-50/60 text-foreground dark:bg-amber-500/10","role":"alert","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"20","height":"20","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"1.75","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0Z"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex-1 [&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em]","children":"Do not move admin or health onto the public listener"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["It is tempting to put ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," on 50051 so a load balancer can probe it. That\nmoves the admin API there too if they share a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"services"}]," block, and it means\nthe health path is the same listener your developers reach. Configure a\nseparate listener if a probe needs a reachable endpoint, and put nothing else\non it."]}]]}]]}]
