26:["$","p",null,{"children":["The name is not a warning about best practice: the certificate expired, and\nits private key is public. Every client that talks to a listener using it must\npass ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--insecure"}]," or equivalent, which is what the repository's own TLS\nintegration test does. That is the only thing these files are for."]}]
27:["$","p",null,{"children":["No certificate-generation script exists anywhere in the tree. You supply real\nmaterial yourself, from whatever your organisation already uses: an internal CA,\ncert-manager in a cluster, or a public CA if the endpoint is genuinely public.\n",["$","$L58",null,{"href":"/how-to/tls-and-auth","children":"TLS and auth"}]," walks through what the client side needs\nonce you have it."]}]
