33:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"use_native_roots: true"}]," trusts the host's system trust store instead of a\nnamed CA. Convenient against a public endpoint, wrong against an internal one:\nit means any publicly-trusted certificate for that hostname is accepted."]}]
34:["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-sandbox-is-not-a-security-boundary","children":"The sandbox is not a security boundary"}]
35:["$","p",null,{"children":["For isolation from state left by an earlier action, development builds offer\nthe opt-in ",["$","$L58",null,{"href":"/reference/forge-config/main#localworkerconfig","children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"single_use"}]," lifecycle"]}],".\nIt requires a launcher that replaces the container and its writable volumes\nafter every action. This prevents reuse of local files, background processes,\nand worker caches. It does not create a new kernel boundary or make untrusted\nactions safe on a privileged container host. Continue applying the network\nand process restrictions described on this page."]}]
36:["$","p",null,{"children":["The development-only\n",["$","$L58",null,{"href":"/reference/forge-config/main#buck2filecaptureconfig","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_buck2_file_capture"}]}],"\noption additionally runs an operator-supplied collector inside that dedicated\nLinux container. Configure it to exclude platform credentials and internal\ncaches, and use narrowly scoped credentials for its ingest service. The hook\ndoes not isolate a token from action processes with the same user privileges.\nThe collector and\nits ingest service must enforce authorization and filesystem boundaries.\nInvocation metadata identifies the client request; it does not authenticate its\nowner. Separate action mount namespaces and entrypoint wrappers are rejected so\nthe collector cannot accidentally archive the outer worker's filesystem."]}]
37:["$","p",null,{"children":["Workers can be configured with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces: true"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace: true"}],". Both are real, and neither makes an action safe to\nrun on your behalf."]}]
38:["$","p",null,{"children":"What the worker actually does before executing an action:"}]
39:["$","$L59",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /></svg>","children":["$","$L5a",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"unshare(CLONE_NEWPID | CLONE_NEWUSER | CLONE_NEWIPC | CLONE_NEWUTS)"}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/setgroups  \"deny\""}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/uid_map    \"<uid> <uid> 1\""}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/gid_map    \"<gid> <gid> 1\""}]}]]}]}]}]
